  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between the compound 2-Methyl-4-oxo-6-(3,7,15-trihydroxy-4,4,10,13,14-pentamethyl-11-oxo-1,2,3,5,6,7,8,9,12,15,16,17-dodecahydrocyclopenta[a]phenanthren-17-yl)heptanoic acid and the CD276 antigen, as it is identified as a target of multiple compounds that ultimately interact with CD276. Specifically, the compound is linked to SK-MEL-2, a melanoma cell line, which is known to be a target of Lagunamide B and Neochamaejasmin A, both of which have been shown to interact with CD276. The consistent presence of the compound as a target of these agents, along with the final scores indicating a moderate level of confidence, suggests that the compound may play a role in modulating CD276 activity. The evidence highlights a pathway where the compound could act as a modulator or inhibitor of CD276, potentially influencing immune responses or tumor progression. The relationship is supported by multiple independent pathways, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains to be elucidated.",
